{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Learn to do well.</b> A verb, and the meaning is להיטב." "<b>Relieve the oppressed.</b> The alef in place of yod, and the opposite of this is תתיימרו (Isaiah 66:6)." "<b>Oppressed</b> is an adjective, like קרוב, from the same root as מעול and חומץ (Psalms 71:4). And R[abbi] interpreted it as: they shall make the judgment sour, and the meaning is that they shall not judge immediately, and the meaning of אשרו is like אשרוני בנות (Genesis 30:13)." "<b>Judge the fatherless.</b> Judge the case of the orphan who has no helper, and similarly שפטני אלהי' וריבה ריבי (Psalms 43:1), and likewise <b>plead for the widow.</b>"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:51:28.255164172Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}